{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type EmbeddingInputItem = \n  | string\n  | TextPart\n  | ImagePart\n  | EmbeddingContentParts;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L3067","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:3067"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One embeddable item, producing exactly one vector. A bare string is\nshorthand for a text part; a nested "},{"type":"link","href":"EmbeddingContentParts.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"EmbeddingContentParts"}]},{"type":"text","value":" array\nfuses its parts into a single vector. Note that a bare array at the top\nlevel of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" is the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"list of items"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (one vector each) — fuse by\nnesting, e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input: [[textPart, imagePart]]"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype EmbeddingInputItem = \n  | string\n  | TextPart\n  | ImagePart\n  | EmbeddingContentParts;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:3067](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L3067)\n\nOne embeddable item, producing exactly one vector. A bare string is\nshorthand for a text part; a nested [EmbeddingContentParts](EmbeddingContentParts.md) array\nfuses its parts into a single vector. Note that a bare array at the top\nlevel of `input` is the *list of items* (one vector each) — fuse by\nnesting, e.g. `input: [[textPart, imagePart]]`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: EmbeddingInputItem\ntitle: EmbeddingInputItem\n---\n\n```ts\ntype EmbeddingInputItem = \n  | string\n  | TextPart\n  | ImagePart\n  | EmbeddingContentParts;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:3067](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L3067)\n\nOne embeddable item, producing exactly one vector. A bare string is\nshorthand for a text part; a nested [EmbeddingContentParts](EmbeddingContentParts.md) array\nfuses its parts into a single vector. Note that a bare array at the top\nlevel of `input` is the *list of items* (one vector each) — fuse by\nnesting, e.g. `input: [[textPart, imagePart]]`.\n"}
